# Line endings are normalised in the repository and checked out as LF.
#
# This is not a style preference. On a Windows checkout without this file, git
# converts every .go file to CRLF, gofmt then reports the whole tree as
# unformatted, and a diff touches every line while hiding the real edit. The
# format gate in ci.yml caught exactly that: green on Linux and macOS, every
# file listed on Windows, with no genuine formatting problem anywhere.
#
# The same applies in reverse. An edit made on Windows and committed without
# this file arrives with CRLF committed into the repository, and gofmt flags
# every line of it on every platform afterward.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.go   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf

# Binaries. text=auto must not touch these, and the release artifacts are
# built rather than committed, so there is nothing to mark here yet. Kept
# explicit so adding a committed binary later does not silently corrupt it.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
*.exe  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.db   binary
